 [
   {
     "heading": "Privacy Policy - Phraseman by Knowly",
-    "body": "Last updated: October 18, 2026\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how Maksym Babiev, an individual trader trading as \"Knowly\" (\"Knowly\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\"), collects, uses, discloses, stores, and deletes information when you use Phraseman (the \"App\"), related cloud features, and Knowly website pages for Phraseman. The data controller is Maksym Babiev, Ardagh, Ballymackerry, V42 P599, Ireland. Privacy contact: support.phraseman@gmail.com.\n\nThis Policy is intended to describe the App's current data practices. If a store listing, in-app notice, or consent screen gives more specific information for a particular platform or feature, that notice also applies."
+    "body": "Last updated: October 21, 2026\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how Maksym Babiev, an individual trader trading as \"Knowly\" (\"Knowly\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\"), collects, uses, discloses, stores, and deletes information when you use Phraseman (the \"App\"), related cloud features, and Knowly website pages for Phraseman. The data controller is Maksym Babiev, Ardagh, Ballymackerry, V42 P599, Ireland. Privacy contact: support.phraseman@gmail.com.\n\nThis Policy is intended to describe the App's current data practices. If a store listing, in-app notice, or consent screen gives more specific information for a particular platform or feature, that notice also applies."
   },
   {
     "heading": "1. Scope, controller, and acceptance",
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
   },
   {
     "heading": "5. Public, social, and historical competitive data",
-    "body": "Some data is visible to other users when you use current public or social features. This may include nickname, coin-rank avatar, profile card settings and style, the short profile-card caption you write yourself (available with a Pro profile card), streak, rank, Peak floor, steps and weekly result, weekly coins earned (shown to members of your Peak room), historical Arena and tournament results from earlier app versions, premium markers, friend activity, activity likes, community pack author information, seller notifications, and similar profile fields. Your profile-card caption is visible to other players who open your profile card; other players can report it, and we may remove captions that break our rules. If you answer the daily poll, we store your chosen option linked to your account ID to prevent repeat voting; other users only see aggregated percentages. When you save a video to your favorites, the App may show other users how many people saved that video; this is an aggregated count only and does not reveal who saved it. Visibility depends on the feature: some fields may be public to app users, some visible to friends, some visible to community pack buyers or sellers, and some visible only to moderators/admins.\n\nThe Peak groups players into weekly rooms of up to 30 places for each study language. Other app users who open the room can see your nickname, avatar and cosmetic style, your steps, place and weekly result. Some places in a room may be filled by computer-controlled participants rather than real people. Weekly room records are kept as part of the Peak history; your entry is removed from them when your account is deleted.\n\nWhen you use the Together feature with friends, those friends may see whether you studied today, how many days you both studied on the same day, the resulting friendship level and progress, Friends may also send or receive nudge signals through this feature.\n\nHistorical records created by retired features (such as the old Quiz mode, Arena matches and friend duels, tournaments, clubs, friend gifts, or the old ideas board (submitted ideas, likes and reports on ideas)), including old results or participation records, may be retained only as reasonably necessary for security, fraud or abuse prevention, dispute handling, legal compliance, backup expiry, or deletion integrity. Account deletion is designed to delete or de-identify those historical records controlled by Knowly, subject only to the limited retention grounds described in this Policy. Those historical records are not presented as currently available gameplay features."
+    "body": "Some data is visible to other users when you use current public or social features. This may include nickname, coin-rank avatar, profile card settings and style, the short profile-card caption you write yourself (available with a Pro profile card), streak, rank, Peak floor, steps and weekly result, weekly coins earned (shown to members of your Peak room), historical Arena and tournament results from earlier app versions, premium markers, friend activity, activity likes, community pack author information, seller notifications, and similar profile fields. Your profile-card caption is visible to other players who open your profile card; other players can report it, and we may remove captions that break our rules. If you answer a poll in the App, we record only which questions your account has already answered, so that you cannot vote twice; the option you choose is added only to aggregated counts and is not stored with your account ID. Your own answers may be kept on your device. Other users only see aggregated results. When you save a video to your favorites, the App may show other users how many people saved that video; this is an aggregated count only and does not reveal who saved it. Visibility depends on the feature: some fields may be public to app users, some visible to friends, some visible to community pack buyers or sellers, and some visible only to moderators/admins.\n\nIf you have Phraseman Plus, other users may see a Plus marker (for example, a ring around your avatar) next to your nickname in friends lists, leaderboards, Peak rooms, and community features. The marker shows only that Plus is currently active; it does not show your plan, price, renewal date, how you got Plus, or any payment details.\n\nThe Peak groups players into weekly rooms of up to 30 places for each study language. Other app users who open the room can see your nickname, avatar and cosmetic style, your steps, place and weekly result. Some places in a room may be filled by computer-controlled participants rather than real people. Weekly room records are kept as part of the Peak history; your entry is removed from them when your account is deleted.\n\nWhen you use the Together feature with friends, those friends may see whether you studied today, which days of the current week you studied, how many days you both studied on the same day — including your shared streak in a row and its best length — the resulting friendship level and progress. Friends may also send or receive nudge signals through this feature.\n\nOnly friends you have accepted (not other users) may also see: in the weekly friend summary, how many study sessions you completed that week, your best day, and your Peak floor; in the shared phrase of the day, the phrase option you chose; in Learn Together and Duel, that you invited them and the result of a duel between the two of you; and, when you send a friend an energy gift, that it came from you.\n\nHistorical records created by retired features (such as the old Quiz mode, Arena matches and friend duels, tournaments, clubs, friend gifts, or the old ideas board (submitted ideas, likes and reports on ideas)), including old results or participation records, may be retained only as reasonably necessary for security, fraud or abuse prevention, dispute handling, legal compliance, backup expiry, or deletion integrity. Account deletion is designed to delete or de-identify those historical records controlled by Knowly, subject only to the limited retention grounds described in this Policy. Those historical records are not presented as currently available gameplay features."
   },
   {
     "heading": "6. User content, community packs, reports, and moderation",
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
   },
   {
     "heading": "14. Website, cookies, leads, and web purchases",
-    "body": "The Knowly website uses local storage and session storage for essential preferences and flows, including theme choice, quiz progress, first-touch UTM attribution, lead email, cached prices, and your Meta Pixel consent choice. It also sends limited website events (page category, visit/view, store clicks, and quiz/checkout funnel events) to our Cloud Function, which stores aggregate counters. To protect that endpoint from abuse, we create a short-lived hash of the visitor IP address for rate limiting; hosting providers may also process IP addresses and request logs.\n\nIf Meta Pixel is enabled, we load it only after opt-in consent in the EU, EEA, UK, and Switzerland. You can accept, reject, or later change that choice using the \"Cookie settings\" link in the website footer.\n\nIf you request a quiz plan by email, we process your email address, quiz answers, UTM attribution, page, consent choice, and delivery/unsubscribe status to send the requested plan. We send follow-up product emails only when you separately opt in; you can withdraw that consent through the unsubscribe link in any such email or by contacting us.\n\nIf you use the website contact form, email support, or legal request channels, we may process your name, email address, message, topic, page URL, user-agent, forwarded IP header, support metadata, account identifiers you provide, and our replies. To respond faster, support messages may be triaged and answered with AI assistance: the text of your message and related support context may be shared with our AI provider (OpenAI) to classify the request and draft a reply, and routine replies may be sent automatically. You can ask for human review in your reply at any time.\n\nFor website purchases, we process your email, selected plan, gift choice, quiz/UTM attribution, order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, activation code, and payment-provider transaction references. Card and PayPal payment credentials are collected by Stripe or PayPal, not by Knowly."
+    "body": "The Knowly website uses local storage and session storage for essential preferences and flows, including theme choice, quiz progress, first-touch UTM attribution, lead email, cached prices, and your Meta Pixel consent choice. It also sends limited website events (page category, visit/view, store clicks, and quiz/checkout funnel events) to our Cloud Function, which stores aggregate counters. To protect that endpoint from abuse, we create a short-lived hash of the visitor IP address for rate limiting; hosting providers may also process IP addresses and request logs.\n\nIf Meta Pixel is enabled, we load it only after opt-in consent in the EU, EEA, UK, and Switzerland. You can accept, reject, or later change that choice using the \"Cookie settings\" link in the website footer.\n\nIf you request a quiz plan by email, we process your email address, quiz answers, UTM attribution, page, consent choice, and delivery/unsubscribe status to send the requested plan. We send follow-up product emails only when you separately opt in; you can withdraw that consent through the unsubscribe link in any such email or by contacting us.\n\nIf you use the website contact form, email support, or legal request channels, we may process your name, email address, message, topic, page URL, user-agent, forwarded IP header, support metadata, account identifiers you provide, and our replies. To respond faster, support messages may be triaged and answered with AI assistance: the text of your message and related support context may be shared with our AI provider (OpenAI) to classify the request and draft a reply, and routine replies may be sent automatically. You can ask for human review in your reply at any time.\n\nFor website purchases, we process your email, selected plan, quiz/UTM attribution, order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, activation code, and payment-provider transaction references.\n\nGifts of Phraseman Plus for another person are sold only on the website. When you buy a gift, we process your email address, the plan, the recipient name and sender name you enter for the certificate, and the delivery method you choose: a code sent to your email or a gift link that you share yourself. We also process order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, the activation code or gift link, and payment-provider transaction references. The certificate, gift email, and gift page show the plan and the names you entered; anyone who opens the gift link can see them. A gift is activated when the recipient enters the code or opens the gift link in the App; we then link the gift to the recipient's account to turn on Plus, or to extend an active Plus period, and to prevent repeated use. You can cancel a code or gift link until it is activated; after cancellation it stops working, and refunds for cancelled gifts are handled manually through support. We do not show the buyer the recipient's account, progress, or other personal data. Card and PayPal payment credentials are collected by Stripe or PayPal, not by Knowly."
   },
